think Crux-first choice between the two doors: line_project is the CRUX. It confronts the one thing every line rung carefully avoided -- DIVISION. The perpendicular foot A + (proj/len2)(B - A) is RATIONAL, whole in doubled coordinates only sometimes. line_corridor_summary is aggregation over already-solved primitives; line_project is the decisive move that, once made, lets a surface name and DRAW the actual nearest point. I approved my own design round.
think The exact-integer answer: hold the foot TIMES len2 as a whole i128 pair, foot_scaled = A*len2 + clamp(proj,0,len2)*(B - A) -- the same clear-the-divide move line_segment_distance made. Verified the identity |foot_scaled - C*len2|^2 == segment_key * len2 by hand on three scene points (M, F, Y) before writing a line -- exact every time, NO float NO square root NO divide.
